  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0158","literal","There was also the Iron-Forbidden State: in Shengzong's Chongxi year 17 it begged troops to assist the attack on Western Xia; the edict refused.","There was also the Iron-Forbidden State: in Xingzong's Chongxi year 17 it begged troops to assist the attack on Western Xia; the edict refused.","Chinese 興宗重熙十七年 names Xingzong; Shengzong (聖宗) is a different Liao emperor, and Chongxi was Xingzong's era.","high","applied"],
    ["s0158","idiomatic","The Iron-Forbidden State once asked in Chongxi year 17 to join an attack on Western Xia; the court denied the request.","In Xingzong's Chongxi year 17 the Iron-Forbidden State once asked to join an attack on Western Xia; the court denied the request.","The Chinese explicitly names 興宗 before 重熙十七年; the idiomatic omits that temple name, and restoring Xingzong matches the source.","high","applied"],
    ["s0222","literal","Goryeo was a small state yet repeatedly cost Liao armies—was it not because its terrain was hard to rely on?","Goryeo was a small state yet repeatedly cost Liao armies—was it not because its difficult terrain was sufficient to rely on?","足恃 means the terrain was sufficient to rely on as a defense; 'hard to rely on' reverses that sense.","high","applied"],
    ["s0220","idiomatic","Only when Song's Taizong attacked Northern Han could Liao not relieve the target; otherwise Liao mostly lost, and wins rarely paid for themselves.","Only when Song's Taizong campaigned against Northern Han could Liao not save it; otherwise Song mostly lost, and even victories did not repay the cost.","遼不能救 correctly means Liao could not rescue Northern Han, but 餘多敗衄 continues the Song subject (clarified by s0221 on China's loss of the five passes); the proposal still wrongly makes Liao the loser.","medium","applied"]
  ],
